>
>## Unify two lists of types pairwise, producing a single substitution that satisfies every pair. The lists must have the same length; the comment is attached to each generated constraint for diagnostics.
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>term unifyTypeLists = λcx,schemaTypes,l,r,comment.let toConstraint := λl,r.typing.TypeConstraint{`left` = l, `right` = r, comment = comment} in unifyTypeConstraints cx schemaTypes (lists.zipWith toConstraint l r)
#^^^^ source.hydra keyword.other.definition.hydra
